{"meta": {"name": "Sunburn device", "cloudId": "pxt/microbit", "editor": "blocksprj", "status": "unpublished", "targetVersions": {"target": "9.0.12", "pxt": "13.0.9"}, "comment": "Sunburn device firmware 3.1: the flowchart as blocks, laid out in 9 labelled sections"}, "source": "{\"main.blocks\": \"<xml xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\\\">\\n<comment id=\\\"note00\\\" x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"640\\\" h=\\\"470\\\">SUNBURN DEVICE  -  micro:bit firmware 3.1\\n\\nHow to read this workspace:\\nThe program is laid out in 9 numbered sections in two rows, left to right. Each section starts with a note like this one.\\nSections 1 and 2 are the whole program: 1 is the settings and start-up, 2 is the flowchart. Sections 3 to 9 are the parts the flowchart calls.\\n\\n 1 Start here: settings      6 Sound and servo\\n 2 The flowchart             7 Bluetooth and serial\\n 3 Buttons                   8 Helpers\\n 4 Alerts                    9 OLED screen driver (optional)\\n 5 Screen and LEDs\\n\\nPins: UV sensor P1, servo P2, buzzer P0 (optional), OLED on I2C P19/P20 (optional).\\nEvery function block has a comment: click the small \\\"?\\\" icon on a block to read what it does.\\nTip: do not use \\\"Format code\\\" or \\\"Clean up blocks\\\" from the workspace menu, that throws this layout away.</comment><comment id=\\\"note01\\\" x=\\\"900\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"480\\\" h=\\\"198\\\">1. START HERE: SETTINGS\\nThe \\\"on start\\\" block. First every setting the program\\nuses (sensor type, servo, screen, UV bands, timings),\\nthen the start-up steps: this is \\\"Device turns on\\\" on\\nthe flowchart. Change your hardware and timings here\\nand nowhere else.</comment><comment id=\\\"note02\\\" x=\\\"1600\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"4915\\\" h=\\\"198\\\">2. THE FLOWCHART\\n\\\"forever\\\" runs runFlowchart again and again. runFlowchart is the whole flowchart from top to bottom: read\\nthe UV sensor, sensor in range?, phone sending online UV?, UV index?, then one of the four branches, wait\\n5 minutes, reapply timer expired?. Every box and decision is a function here with the same name, in the\\nsame order as the flowchart. Read them top to bottom, column by column.</comment><comment id=\\\"note03\\\" x=\\\"6735\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"480\\\" h=\\\"198\\\">3. BUTTONS\\nA = done (sunscreen is on / going inside). A also skips\\na message scrolling on the LEDs, and while waiting it\\nshows the UV index and the countdown. B = wake from\\nstandby. A+B = device turns off, or on again.</comment><comment id=\\\"note04\\\" x=\\\"7435\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"1090\\\" h=\\\"198\\\">4. ALERTS\\nFlash and beep, tap the arm with the servo, and standby. Each one keeps going until A is pressed (or the\\napp sends \\\"ack\\\"), the device is turned off, or its time limit runs out.</comment><comment id=\\\"note05\\\" x=\\\"8745\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" w=\\\"2298\\\" h=\\\"198\\\">5. SCREEN AND LEDS\\nWhat the 5x5 LEDs show, and what the optional OLED screen shows: the UV number, the band, messages and\\nthe countdowns. Messages scroll across the LEDs when there is no OLED.</comment><comment id=\\\"note06\\\" x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"3085\\\" w=\\\"485\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">6. SOUND AND SERVO\\nBeeps on the V2 speaker (or a buzzer on P0), and the\\nservo on P2 whose arm taps the wrist.</comment><comment id=\\\"note07\\\" x=\\\"745\\\" y=\\\"3085\\\" w=\\\"3588\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">7. BLUETOOTH AND SERIAL\\nTalks to the phone app (Bluetooth UART) and to the USB serial console with the same text lines.\\nOut every 2 s:  st=wait;uv=7.3;sen=7.1;onl=6.5;band=vhigh;spf=5400;spfn=3;fw=3.1\\nOut on events:  ev=on  ev=off  ev=sunscreen  ev=reapply  ev=inside  ev=standby  ev=error\\nIn (one per line):  uv=6.5   ack   zero   cal=7   demo=1   power=0   debug=1   ping   read</comment><comment id=\\\"note08\\\" x=\\\"4553\\\" y=\\\"3085\\\" w=\\\"2705\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">8. HELPERS\\nSmall tools used by the rest: sensor presets, the timings, sorting, number and time formatting, tidying\\nup commands, and the debug lines (send debug=1 to see them).</comment><comment id=\\\"note09\\\" x=\\\"7478\\\" y=\\\"3085\\\" w=\\\"5713\\\" h=\\\"176\\\">9. OLED SCREEN DRIVER (optional)\\nOnly used if you add a 128x64 I2C screen (SSD1306 or SH1106) on P19/P20. Draws text on it without needing\\nan extension. The program detects the screen at start-up and works exactly the same without one. You\\nshould not need to change anything here.</comment><block id=\\\"xRRgvHNlG#rZ^u`HECiY\\\" type=\\\"pxt-on-start\\\" x=\\\"900\\\" y=\\\"288\\\">\\n<statement name=\\\"HANDLER\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"Yhu{GP5Kl;kn|E~a:x49\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvSensorType</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"26:X==0sjLnU3^D0|:EH\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvSampleCount</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">15</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\":x7#Xosz^i):aQda5_5s\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">soundOutput</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"Zd-!B0V{LjLiN]g1axtl\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">servoType</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\":*mBp0-;=%tSjDnHs1..\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">servoRestAngle</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">90</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"3r7?/TXdS/f7w$isiKj5\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">servoTapAngle</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">30</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"2if;f1`Awh+IpV:Gk?:J\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">oledMode</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\")]n`YIK:z18E(_~Zfuj(\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">oledType</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">1</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"wjzz9dKrWi:MOn[5ZIV9\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">oledAddress</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">60</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"Bu+q8^)h3+-/#EdTlb,$\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvLowMax</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">2</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"hYYOOHg55On$[5lDHD]|\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvHighMax</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">7</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"Bx-9$eX`*Ixfs:C41$)]\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">uvVeryHighMax</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">10</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"2Pp9},21[mtOCMx9k0_3\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">waitMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">5</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"YWZIiIUH2Y*8ivM)`2n2\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">reapplyHours</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">2</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"SY(Xmlm0wGn4;L__oR2p\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">tapMaxMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">2</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"gWZ.AULoh^r|l!8Y~ctu\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">alertGiveUpMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">10</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"A0!(EQG!|fCq|8mY)w`F\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">onlineUvMaxAgeMinutes</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">30</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"0Xv`5,TnNhx3@9i[R~#H\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">sensorRetrySeconds</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NUM\\\">5</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"uqLT(pSX8%j6t_E{?zX2\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">firmwareVersion</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\"><field name=\\\"NUM\\\">0</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"text\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"TEXT\\\">3.1</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"PrX4?N}xHr#?t*zE8o-|\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"applySensorPreset\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"Yd9v+7|=73%U8bvcaD0q\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"applyTimings\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"OQ~LtI.-k^}R6]:HhYP[\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"setupSound\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"{-G%BMj=I26kHqj`AYUM\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"setupOled\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"OY-]!vnn*o%K(9/.E$3?\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"advertiseOverBluetooth\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"t.+O|8q@D9mpuuWtma,Q\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"0\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"device_get_button2\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"NAME\\\">Button.B</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"e:{.:MWzMC8F%`9@$_6+\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">demoMode</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\"><field name=\\\"NUM\\\">0</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"N:a89gbuk,Y1v34(D5rW\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"applyTimings\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"=eLQKvVq~]S+X+fw}0:Y\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"deviceTurnsOn\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Hold B while switching on for demo timings: 10 s waits and a 1 minute sunscreen timer</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">----- Device turns on -----</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Safety limits: how long an alert beeps before giving up, and how long a\\nvalue from the phone counts as \\\"the phone is sending online UV\\\"</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Timings from the flowchart</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">UV bands from the flowchart (WHO scale), tested on the rounded UV index:\\n0-2 low, 3-7 moderate / high, 8-10 very high, 11+ extreme</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">I2C address: 60 = 0x3C (usual), 61 = 0x3D</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">1 = SSD1306 (most 0.96\\\" screens), 2 = SH1106 (most 1.3\\\" screens)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">OLED screen on the I2C pins (optional).  0 = no screen, 1 = detect it, 2 = always on</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Angles for a positional servo: resting, and the tap</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Servo on P2: 1 = normal positional servo, 2 = continuous rotation servo</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Sound: 1 = micro:bit V2 speaker, 2 = buzzer on P0 (a V1 always uses P0)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">One reading is the middle value of this many samples (kills noise spikes)</comment>\\n</block>\\n</next>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">UV sensor on P1.  1 = GUVA-S12SD / Crowtail / Grove / DFRobot / ElecFreaks\\n2 = ML8511 (SparkFun, Adafruit)   3 = sensors sold as \\\"0-1023 = UV 0-15\\\"</comment>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">START HERE. Settings first (change these to match your parts), then the start-up steps: sensor maths, timings, sound, screen, Bluetooth, then \\\"Device turns on\\\". Hold B while switching on for demo timings.</comment></block>\\n<block id=\\\"kpm+5SHf2+;rMJlJ;4(|\\\" type=\\\"device_forever\\\" x=\\\"1600\\\" y=\\\"288\\\">\\n<statement name=\\\"HANDLER\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"slSM-Me7[G{BjIE?kj@4\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block type=\\\"variables_get\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">deviceOn</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"zbBjC_)sxy-jC0#miVz=\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"runFlowchart\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<statement name=\\\"ELSE\\\">\\n<block id=\\\".T:wj%}J1FGE*r#FbCz}\\\" type=\\\"device_pause\\\">\\n<value name=\\\"pause\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"timePicker\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"ms\\\">500</field>\\n</shadow>\\n</value>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n</block>\\n</statement>\\n<comment pinned=\\\"false\\\">Forever: one trip around the flowchart, then straight back to \\\"Read UV sensor\\\"</comment>\\n</block>\\n<block id=\\\"}[Uw-}M`+y8X9s)~CThE\\\" type=\\\"function_definition\\\" x=\\\"1600\\\" y=\\\"636\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"runFlowchart\\\">\\n</mutation>\\n<statement name=\\\"STACK\\\">\\n<block id=\\\"7VBHjPKg;;EOM$yGT~i6\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"readUvSensor\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"JMC}`CW$3.aqi*b^%fb%\\\" type=\\\"controls_if\\\">\\n<mutation elseif=\\\"0\\\" else=\\\"1\\\" />\\n<value name=\\\"IF0\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"logic_boolean\\\"><field name=\\\"BOOL\\\">TRUE</field></shadow>\\n<block id=\\\"WiXWgGQto7b]Gp^yvWe$\\\" type=\\\"function_call_output\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"sensorReadingInRange\\\" />\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<statement name=\\\"DO0\\\">\\n<block id=\\\":|~UOfbeT^PXre#=T7+8\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"chooseUvValue\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"4Am$~H!n[cl)FL}i0b58\\\" type=\\\"function_call\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"showUvReading\\\" />\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"f9m0eD3}10P9Qn4B49sP\\\" type=\\\"variables_set\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">currentBand</field>\\n<value name=\\\"VALUE\\\">\\n<shadow type=\\\"math_number\\\"><field name=\\\"NUM\\\">0</field></shadow>\\n<block id=\\\"%sUb~5^O8jcoo~pTi8k-\\\" type=\\\"function_call_output\\\">\\n<mutation name=\\\"uvBand\\\">\\n<arg name=\\\"uv\\\" type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"fwinntrguorjno4i050v9j\\\" />\\n</mutation>\\n<value name=\\\"fwinntrguorjno4i050v9j\\\">\\n<block type=\\\"variables_get\\\">\\n<field name=\\\"VAR\\\">currentUv</field>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n</block>\\n</value>\\n<next>\\n<block id=\\\"`m:P6eBf0^